<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Product Instructions</title>
    <style>
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
        .page {
            width: 794px; height: 1123px;
            padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
            overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
            position: relative;
            font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
        }
        .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
        h1, h2, h3 { font-weight: bold; }
        table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; }
        td { padding: 5px 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
            <div style="width: 45%;">
                <h1 style="font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 10px;">DA-LITE®</h1>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">A <span data-field="company_name">{{ company_name }}</span> Brand</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">{{ company_address_line_1 }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">{{ company_address_line_2 }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">P: {{ company_phone }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">F: {{ company_fax }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">E: {{ company_email }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 12px;">W: {{ company_website }}</p>
                <p style="font-size: 10px; margin-top: 30px;">DL-0331 (Rev {{ revision_number }})</p>
                <p style="font-size: 10px;">© {{ copyright_year }} <span data-field="company_name">{{ company_name }}</span> LLC. Printed in U.S.A.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 10px; text-align: right;">{{ document_number }}</p>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 50%; text-align: right;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 20px;">INSTRUCTIONS FOR</h2>
                <h1 style="font-size: 36px; margin-top: 0;">Model {{ model_number_1 }} And {{ model_number_2 }}</h1>
                <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">Project-O-Stands</h2>
                <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
                    <img src="placeholder_image_stand_1.png" alt="Product Image" style="width: 300px; height: auto;">
                </div>
                <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
                    <img src="placeholder_logo.png" alt="DA-LITE Logo" style="width: 150px; height: auto;">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
            <div style="width: 50%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 20px;">Set-Up Instructions</h2>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">Remove all four legs from the rubber leg holder and screw into threaded inserts.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">To adjust leg length, loosen the Sure-Grip Camlock Collars, adjust to desired table height and tighten collar.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 20px;"><strong>NOTE:</strong> The non-skid platform supports up to {{ weight_capacity }} lbs. with legs completely extended.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 14px;">To take down and store your Project-O-Stand, adjust legs to shortest length, remove from table top and slip into rubber leg holder.</p>
                <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 15px;"><strong>NOTE:</strong> Place legs into center slots of leg holder first, then place legs into outside slots.</p>

                <div style="margin-top: 40px;">
                    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;">
                        <div style="width: 50%;">
                            <img src="placeholder_diagram_view_a.png" alt="View A Diagram" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                            <p style="font-size: 12px; text-align: center; margin-top: 5px;">View A</p>
                        </div>
                        <div style="width: 45%;">
                            <p style="font-size: 14px;">Model {{ model_number_2 }} Only</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 10px;">Adjust all 4 legs to desired length before assembling to the table.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="width: 50%;">
                <h2 style="font-size: 20px;">Accessories</h2>
                <div style="margin-bottom: 30px;">
                    <h3 style="font-size: 16px;">Model {{ model_number_1 }}</h3>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px;"><strong>Accessory Shelf</strong></p>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px;">Convenient {{ shelf_size }} shelf may be used on all Project-O-Stands to create a convenient storage place for dissolve units, trays, cassettes, and presentation materials. Shelf is made of wood composition board with plastic laminate top and vinyl edges.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 style="font-size: 16px;">Model {{ model_number_2 }}</h3>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px;"><strong>Piggy Back Stand</strong></p>
                    <p style="font-size: 14px;">Aluminum rack may be securely attached to Model {{ model_number_2 }} Project-O-Stand and allows an additional EKTAGRAPHIC® projector to be stacked above the base unit. Projector legs drop into vinyl leg cups with adjustable spacing. Unit folds flat for storage and transportation.</p>
                </div>
                <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
                    <img src="placeholder_diagram_view_b.png" alt="View B Diagram" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="page">
        <div style="width: 100%;">
            <h2 style="font-size: 20px;">Care Instructions</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 14px;">Your new Project-O-Stand requires very little care. Dust as needed with a soft cloth; if required, use mild soap and water to clean off stubborn spots. Abrasive cleaners should be avoided as they may scratch the legs on both models.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>